# care_fe route/entry-point survey (branch `bodhi/questionnaire-wysiwyg-builder`)

## 1. `src/Routers/routes/ConsultationRoutes.tsx` — COMPLETE route map

Note: `EncounterQuestionnaire` no longer exists on this branch; every fill route renders `QuestionnaireFillPage` (default export of `src/components/QuestionnaireV2/fill/QuestionnaireFillPage.tsx`).

Exact routes and rendered elements:

| Route path (verbatim) | Element + props |
|---|---|
| `/facility/:facilityId/patient/:patientId/prescription/:prescriptionId/print` | `<PrintPrescription facilityId patientId prescriptionId />` |
| `/facility/:facilityId/patient/:patientId/encounter/:encounterId/prescriptions/print` | `<PrintPrescription facilityId patientId encounterId />` |
| 7 paths via reduce: `/facility/:facilityId/patient/:patientId/encounter/:encounterId/questionnaire/:questionnaireId/responses/print`, `/organization/:organizationId/patient/:patientId/encounter/:encounterId/questionnaire/:questionnaireId/responses/print`, `/facility/:facilityId/patient/:patientId/questionnaire/:questionnaireId/responses/print`, `/organization/:organizationId/patient/:patientId/questionnaire/:questionnaireId/responses/print`, `/patient/:patientId/questionnaire/:questionnaireId/responses/print`, `/facility/:facilityId/patient/:patientId/history/questionnaire/:questionnaireId/responses/print`, `/patient/:patientId/history/questionnaire/:questionnaireId/responses/print` | `<PrintAllQuestionnaireResponses encounterId patientId questionnaireId facilityId />` |
| 7 paths via reduce: `/facility/:facilityId/patient/:patientId/encounter/:encounterId/questionnaire_response/:questionnaireResponseId/print`, `/facility/:facilityId/patient/:patientId/history/questionnaire_response/:questionnaireResponseId/print`, `/patient/:patientId/history/questionnaire_response/:questionnaireResponseId/print`, `/organization/:organizationId/patient/:patientId/encounter/:encounterId/questionnaire_response/:questionnaireResponseId/print`, `/facility/:facilityId/patient/:patientId/questionnaire_response/:questionnaireResponseId/print`, `/organization/:organizationId/patient/:patientId/questionnaire_response/:questionnaireResponseId/print`, `/patient/:patientId/questionnaire_response/:questionnaireResponseId/print` | `<PrintQuestionnaireResponse encounterId patientId questionnaireResponseId facilityId />` |
| `/facility/:facilityId/patient/:patientId/encounter/:encounterId/type/:productType/administrations/print` | `<PrintMedicationAdministration facilityId encounterId patientId productType={productType as AdministrableProductType} />` |
| `/facility/:facilityId/patient/:patientId/encounter/:encounterId/report/template/:templateSlug` | `<ReportViewer encounterId templateSlug />` |
| `/facility/:facilityId/patient/:patientId/encounter/:encounterId/report/:reportId` | `<ReportViewer encounterId reportId />` |
| `/facility/:facilityId/patient/:patientId/encounter/:encounterId/questionnaire` | `<QuestionnaireFillPage facilityId encounterId patientId subjectType="encounter" />` |
| `/facility/:facilityId/patient/:patientId/encounter/:encounterId/questionnaire/:questionnaireId` | `<QuestionnaireFillPage facilityId encounterId questionnaireId patientId subjectType="encounter" />` |
| `/facility/:facilityId/patient/:patientId/encounter/:encounterId/questionnaire_response/:id` | `<QuestionnaireResponseView responseId={id} patientId />` |
| 2 paths via reduce over `["facility", "organization"]`: `/facility/:id/patient/:patientId/encounter/:encounterId/:tab` and `/organization/:id/patient/:patientId/encounter/:encounterId/:tab` | `<EncounterProvider encounterId patientId facilityId={identifier === "facility" ? id : undefined}><EncounterShow tab={tab} /></EncounterProvider>` |
| `/facility/:facilityId/patient/:patientId/consultation` | `<QuestionnaireFillPage facilityId patientId questionnaireId="encounter" subjectType="encounter" />` |
| `/facility/:facilityId/patient/:patientId/questionnaire` | `<QuestionnaireFillPage facilityId patientId subjectType="patient" />` |
| `/facility/:facilityId/patient/:patientId/questionnaire/:questionnaireId` | `<QuestionnaireFillPage facilityId patientId questionnaireId subjectType="patient" />` |
| `/patient/:patientId/questionnaire` | `<QuestionnaireFillPage patientId subjectType="patient" />` |
| `/patient/:patientId/questionnaire/:questionnaireId` | `<QuestionnaireFillPage patientId questionnaireId subjectType="patient" />` |

`QuestionnaireFillPage` props interface (from `src/components/QuestionnaireV2/fill/QuestionnaireFillPage.tsx`):

```typescript
interface FillPageProps {
  facilityId?: string;
  patientId: string;
  encounterId?: string;
  questionnaireId?: string;
  subjectType?: string;
}
```

Its exit target helper (relevant to new mounts — currently patient-centric only):

```typescript
function exitTargetFor({ facilityId, patientId, encounterId }: FillPageProps): string {
  if (encounterId && facilityId) {
    return `/facility/${facilityId}/patient/${patientId}/encounter/${encounterId}/updates`;
  }
  if (facilityId) {
    return `/facility/${facilityId}/patient/${patientId}/updates`;
  }
  return `/patient/${patientId}/updates`;
}
```

Data fetching inside FillPage: fetches questionnaire by id (`questionnaireApi.get`), encounter (`encounterApi.get`, enabled `!!encounterId`), patient (`patientApi.get`, enabled `!encounterId`), server draft (`formSubmissionApi.get` when `?continue_draft=` present). `patient = encounter?.patient ?? fetchedPatient`. Draft scope `subjectKey: encounterId ?? patientId`.

## 2. Location pages (two distinct areas)

### 2a. Settings-side location management (CRUD)
- Directory: `/Users/bodhishthomas/code/care_fe/src/pages/Facility/settings/locations/` — `LocationSettings.tsx`, `LocationView.tsx`, `LocationForm.tsx`, `LocationSheet.tsx`, `LocationImport.tsx`, `LocationMap.tsx`, `components/LocationCard.tsx`, `components/LocationTable.tsx`.
- Routes (registered in `src/pages/Facility/settings/layout.tsx`, mounted under basePath `/facility/:facilityId/settings` via raviger `useRoutes(..., { basePath })`):
  - `"/locations"` → `<LocationSettings facilityId />` (full URL `/facility/:facilityId/settings/locations`)
  - `"/locations/import"` → `<LocationImport facilityId />`
  - `"/locations/:id"` → `<LocationSettings facilityId locationId={id} />` (full URL `/facility/:facilityId/settings/locations/:id`)
- `LocationSettings` renders a left tree sidebar (`LocationTreeNode` from `@/pages/Facility/locations/LocationNavbar`) + either the list/table or, when `locationId` is set, `<LocationView id={locationId} facilityId isNested onBackToParent onSelectLocation />`.
- `LocationView.tsx` props:
  ```typescript
  interface Props {
    id: string;
    facilityId: string;
    isNested?: boolean;
    onBackToParent?: () => void;
    onSelectLocation?: (location: LocationRead) => void;
  }
  ```
  Structure: `<Breadcrumb>` (Home → ancestor chain) → `<Page hideTitleOnPage title={location?.name}>` → header block: `<h2>{location.name}</h2>` + `location_form__{form}` Badge + status Badge, then an action row containing a search `<Input>` and a button group (`Add Location` button shown when `location.mode === "kind"`, plus `LinkDepartmentsSheet` trigger button "Manage organization"). **Mount point for a 'Fill questionnaire' entry:** this button group (`div.flex.flex-col.lg:flex-row.gap-2` around lines 237–270 of `LocationView.tsx`) — it already holds sibling action buttons and has `facilityId` + location `id` in scope.

### 2b. Operational location workspace (has its own sub-router)
- Directory: `/Users/bodhishthomas/code/care_fe/src/pages/Facility/locations/` — `LocationLayout.tsx`, `LocationList.tsx`, `LocationContent.tsx`, `LocationNavbar.tsx`, `BedsList.tsx`.
- Top-level route in `src/Routers/routes/FacilityRoutes.tsx`:
  - `"/facility/:facilityId/locations/:locationId*"` → `<LocationLayout facilityId locationId />`
- `LocationLayout` runs raviger `useRoutes(getRoutes(facilityId, locationId), { basePath: `/facility/${facilityId}/locations/${locationId}`, routeProps: { facilityId, locationId } })`. Registered sub-paths (relative): `/beds`, `/medication_requests`, `/medication_dispense`, `/medication_return`, `/service_requests`, `/service_requests/:serviceRequestId`, `/inventory/...` (many), `/schedule`, `/appointments`, `/appointments/:appointmentId`, `/queues`, `/queues/:queueId/ongoing`, `/queues/:queueId/completed`, plus `"*"` → `<ErrorPage />`. **Adding a location-scoped fill route here** = add e.g. `"/questionnaire"` / `"/questionnaire/:questionnaireId"` to `getRoutes` in `LocationLayout.tsx` (full URL shape `/facility/:facilityId/locations/:locationId/questionnaire/:questionnaireId`). Note the layout renders no shared chrome itself — just `<div>{routeResult}</div>`; each sub-page composes `LocationContent`/`LocationNavbar` itself.

## 3. Device pages

- Directory: `/Users/bodhishthomas/code/care_fe/src/pages/Facility/settings/devices/` — `DevicesList.tsx`, `DeviceShow.tsx`, `CreateDevice.tsx`, `UpdateDevice.tsx`, `DeviceEncounterHistory.tsx`, `components/` (DeviceCard, DeviceForm, ManageLocationSheet, DeviceSelector, DeviceServiceHistory, EncounterOverviewDevices, etc.), `hooks/usePluginDevices.ts`.
- Routes (same settings layout, basePath `/facility/:facilityId/settings`):
  - `"/devices"` → `<DevicesList facilityId />`
  - `"/devices/create"` → `<CreateDevice facilityId />`
  - `"/devices/:id"` → `<DeviceDetail facilityId deviceId={id} />` (component file `DeviceShow.tsx`, default export `DeviceShow`; full URL `/facility/:facilityId/settings/devices/:id`)
  - `"/devices/:id/edit"` → `<UpdateDevice facilityId deviceId={id} />`
- `DeviceShow` props: `interface Props { facilityId: string; deviceId: string; }`. Structure: `div.max-w-4xl.mx-auto` → header row (`DeviceTypeIcon` + `PageTitle title={device.registered_name}`) → `Card` "device_information" whose `CardHeader` is `flex flex-row justify-between items-center` containing `CardTitle` + an Edit button (`<Link href={`/devices/${deviceId}/edit`}>` — raviger links inside settings inherit the `/facility/:facilityId/settings` basePath from context). **Mount point for 'Fill questionnaire':** either next to that Edit button in the CardHeader, or in the top header row beside `PageTitle`. `device` (type `DeviceDetail` from `@/types/device/device`) is in scope, including `device.current_location` and `device.current_encounter` (with `.facility.id` and `.patient.id`).

## 4. `src/Routers/AppRouter.tsx` structure

- Route maps are plain objects (`AppRoutes = { [path: string]: RouteFunction }`) spread together:
  ```typescript
  const Routes: AppRoutes = {
    "/": () => <UserDashboard />,
    ...ConsultationRoutes,
    ...FacilityRoutes,
    ...PatientRoutes,
    ...ResourceRoutes,
    ...ScheduleRoutes,
    ...UserRoutes,
    ...OrganizationRoutes,
    "/session-expired": () => <SessionExpired />,
    "/not-found": () => <ErrorPage />,
    "/icons": () => <IconIndex />,
    "/licenses": () => <LicensesPage />,
    ...(import.meta.env.PROD ? { "/icons": () => <IconIndex /> } : {}),
  };
  ```
- At render: `routes = { ...pluginRoutes, ...organizationRoutes, ...routes }` then `useRoutes(routes)`; separately `useRoutes(AdminRouter)` (spread of `AdminRoutes`) and `useRoutes(publicRedirects)` (every `PublicRouter` path redirected to `/`). Page = `appPages || adminPages || publicRedirectsPages || <ErrorPage />`.
- `PublicRouter` (`src/Routers/PublicRouter.tsx`) exports its `routes`; AppRouter (authenticated) turns those paths into `<Redirect to="/" />`. Router selection by auth state happens above AppRouter (in the providers), not inside it.
- Sidebar suppression: `PATHS_WITHOUT_SIDEBAR` array mixes exact strings and regexes. Questionnaire-relevant entries (verbatim):
  ```typescript
  // Questionnaire fill routes (fullscreen v2 fill experience)
  /^\/facility\/[^/]+\/patient\/[^/]+\/encounter\/[^/]+\/questionnaire(\/[^/]+)?$/,
  /^\/facility\/[^/]+\/patient\/[^/]+\/questionnaire(\/[^/]+)?$/,
  /^\/facility\/[^/]+\/patient\/[^/]+\/consultation$/,
  /^\/patient\/[^/]+\/questionnaire(\/[^/]+)?$/,
  // Questionnaire studio (fullscreen builder) routes
  /^\/facility\/[^/]+\/settings\/questionnaires\/[^/]+\/edit$/,
  /^\/admin\/questionnaires\/[^/]+\/edit$/,
  ```
  Any new fullscreen fill mount (location/device subject) needs its own regex added here.
- Everything renders inside `SidebarProvider > PermissionProvider > main#pages > div.p-3.mt-4[data-cui-page] > ErrorBoundary`.

## 5. Existing fill-navigation URL shapes

- `src/pages/Encounters/tabs/overview/quick-actions.tsx` — relative hrefs via raviger `<Link basePath={basePath} href={href}>` (basePath prop optional; rendered inside encounter tab so relative to current encounter URL): `questionnaire/allergy_intolerance`, `questionnaire/service_request`, `questionnaire/medication_request`, `questionnaire/symptom`, `questionnaire/diagnosis`. The "Forms" tile opens `FormDialog` with `subjectType="encounter"`.
- `src/pages/Encounters/tabs/overview/FormsDialog.tsx` — on select: `navigate(`/facility/${facilityId}/patient/${patientId}/encounter/${encounterId}/questionnaire/${questionnaire.id}`)`. Lists via `query.debounced(questionnaireApi.list, ...)` keyed `["questionnaires", search, subjectType]`; favorites via `["questionnaire-favorites", facilityId]`.
- `src/pages/Encounters/tabs/overview/FavoriteFormsQuickActions.tsx` — `href={`/facility/${facilityId}/patient/${patientId}/encounter/${encounterId}/questionnaire/${form.id}`}`.
- `src/components/Encounter/EncounterCommandDialog.tsx` — `buildEncounterUrl(path)` = `` `/facility/${encounter.facility.id}/patient/${encounter.patient.id}/encounter/${currentEncounterIdToUse}${path}` `` (plus optional `?selectedEncounter=` param). Used as `navigate(buildEncounterUrl("/questionnaire/service_request"))`, `.../questionnaire/medication_request`, `.../questionnaire/allergy_intolerance`, `.../questionnaire/symptom`, `.../questionnaire/diagnosis`, `.../questionnaire/encounter`, and dynamic `navigate(buildEncounterUrl(`/questionnaire/${questionnaireId}`))` for action ids shaped `questionnaire-<id>`.
- `src/components/Patient/PatientDetailsTab/patientUpdates.tsx` — "Add patient updates" button: `href={facilityId ? `/facility/${facilityId}/patient/${patientId}/questionnaire` : `/patient/${patientId}/questionnaire`}`.

## 6. `src/pages/Facility/settings/layout.tsx` — QuestionnaireScope injection

- `SettingsLayout({ facilityId })` builds `basePath = `/facility/${facilityId}/settings`` and calls `useRoutes(getRoutes(facilityId), { basePath, routeProps: { facilityId } })`, wrapped in `div.container.mx-auto.p-4`.
- Questionnaire pages receive `scope` constructed inline per route, e.g.:
  ```typescript
  "/questionnaires": () => (
    <QuestionnaireListPage
      scope={{
        authContext: "facility",
        facilityId,
        basePath: `/facility/${facilityId}/settings/questionnaires`,
      }}
    />
  ),
  ```
  Same shape for `"/questionnaires/new"` (`QuestionnaireCreatePage`), `"/questionnaires/:id/edit"` (`QuestionnaireStudioPage`, extra prop `id`), `"/questionnaires/:id/versions/:revisionId"` (`QuestionnaireRevisionPage`, props `id`, `revisionId`), `"/questionnaires/:id"` (`QuestionnaireDetailPage`, prop `id`). Ordering comments note raviger matches in object-registration order, so `new`/`:id/edit`/`:id/versions/...` are registered before `":id"`, and a `"*": () => <ErrorPage />` catch-all is last.
- `QuestionnaireScope` type (from `src/types/questionnaire/questionnaire.ts`):
  ```typescript
  export type QuestionnaireScope = {
    /** e.g. `/facility/{id}/settings/questionnaires` or `/admin/questionnaires` */
    basePath: string;
  } & (
    | { authContext: "instance"; facilityId?: undefined; facilityOrganizationId?: undefined }
    | { authContext: "facility"; facilityId: string; facilityOrganizationId?: undefined }
    | { authContext: "facility_organization"; facilityId?: undefined; facilityOrganizationId: string }
    | { authContext: "user"; facilityId: string; facilityOrganizationId?: undefined }
  );
  ```

## 7. Patient banner components

### `src/components/Patient/PatientHeader.tsx`
```typescript
export function PatientHeader({
